        "blast_url": "https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi?PAGE_TYPE=BlastSearch&PROG_DEF=blastn&BLAST_SPEC=GDH_GCA_975146385.1",
        "comments": "The assembly daTeuBotr5.1 is based on 26x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and chloroplast genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, the primary assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Order and orientation of scaffolds is unsure in the centromeric regions of the following scaffolds: Chromosome 1 between\n9.01-9.20Mb, Chromosome 2 between\n5.33-5.60Mb, Chromosome 3 between\n8.72-8.93Mb, Chromosome 4 between\n4.49-5.36Mb, Chromosome 5 between 7.76-8.43Mb, Chromosome 7 between\n6.93-7.17Mb, Chromosome 8 between\n3.08-3.17Mb, Chromosome 11 between\n5.11-5.51Mb, Chromosome 12 between\n7.46-7.64Mb, Chromosome 14 between\n5.95-6.90Mb and Chromosome 16 between\n5.71-6.16Mb. This sample demostrates a very high level of homozygosity between haplotypes as such the primary haplotype represents the haploid assembly of 16 choromosomes whereas the alternative haplotype is incomplete as it was not possible to seperate the two haplotypes during the assembly process.",
